  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **See America Right** (1 review): The reviewer calls this the best version of the song they have ever heard [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **I Put A Spell On You (Screamin' Jay Hawkins cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Jam Eater Blues**: back after 37 archived shows (1833 days); rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **I Will Survive (Gloria Gaynor cover)**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **I Miss The War (John Vanderslice)**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Terror Song (Furniture Huschle cover)**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **2004-10-15-sbd-the-mountain-goats-the-social-orlando-fl** (recommended): soundboard; 17 songs; 64 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- John Vanderslice and the band hit the stage, kicking the show into overdrive [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **2004-10-15-sbd-the-mountain-goats-the-social-orlando-fl**: taped by damorecordo [1]",
